From 60a7aca4ee437fdcd959ba0a940b239b386087a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devin AI <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:22:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Send game state over WebRTC data channels with WebSocket
 fallback

Clients negotiate a peer connection over the existing WebSocket. While a game is
running, position/angle updates go over an unreliable, unordered 'state' channel
(sequenced, stale packets dropped) and player inputs over a reliable ordered 'input'
channel, avoiding TCP head-of-line blocking. Uses optional node-datachannel on the
server; disable with CURVYTRON_WEBRTC=0, configure ICE with CURVYTRON_ICE_SERVERS.

Co-Authored-By: Akshat Bubna <akshatb42@gmail.com>
